# OksaSDR tour, iPad landscape 1366x1024 (QT_SCALE_FACTOR 1.40625: frames 1921x1440), --connect 192.168.0.40.
# On a 20 m SSB station for the sound, English-speaking (M7KOD POTA, 14.219 USB, -98 dBm on 2026-11-13 14:40, its
# voice band filling the passband: the dial on its carrier), phone with the 2.9 kHz receive filter; put back on 14.074 DIGU.
# Captions: "caption # T" a chapter, "caption [box x,y,w,h] text" (frame px), "caption !mark x,y",
# "caption !speed N", "caption !cut" / "!uncut", "caption -" clears. Receive only.
pin 5
ready
freq 14.219
mode USB
span 10
wait 1500
popup filterChooser
wait 1200
taptext 2.9k
wait 1200
close
wait 1500
record 15
caption # Getting started
caption Four short hints show the gestures that cannot be seen: they come by themselves the first time, and View › Hints › Show again brings them back.
taptext Show again
wait 3500
tapname hintsNext
wait 3500
tapname hintsNext
wait 3500
tapname hintsNext
wait 3500
tapname hintsNext
wait 1500
caption Disconnect goes back to the Connect page.
taptext Disconnect
wait 3500
caption The Connect page: radios on this network, your SmartLink radios once you sign in, and radios kept by IP address or host name.
wait 6500
caption + Add a radio keeps one by its IP address or host name: a dynamic DNS name, or Tailscale over a VPN.
tapname addRadio
wait 5000
close
wait 1000
caption Check the connection tests the way to a radio that cannot be reached.
tapname checkConnection
wait 6500
close
wait 1000
caption One tap on a radio connects.
tapname savedRadio0
caption !speed 3
ready
caption !speed 1
caption -
caption !speed 3
span 10
wait 9000
caption !speed 1
caption # The main screen
caption [box 10,82,480,120] The frequency of the active slice. Tap it to type a frequency.
wait 4500
caption [box 488,82,170,125] The mode, and the tuning step under it.
wait 4000
caption [box 692,90,620,52] The slice: its letter, TX on the transmitting slice, the RX and TX antennas, filter, AGC, volume, tuning lock, record and play.
wait 6500
caption [box 700,152,490,48] The radio's noise and notch filters, lit when on. Tap them for the filter and DSP choices.
wait 4000
caption [box 14,232,1366,82] Bands: one tap. The radio's band stack remembers where you were on each.
wait 4500
caption [box 16,328,300,198] Two meters, the S-meter and the radio's voltage here. Tap a meter to choose it.
wait 5000
caption [box 546,328,304,82] A chip for every slice: tap to make it active, press and hold for Make TX slice and Close slice.
wait 5500
caption [box 16,530,1362,522] Spectrum and waterfall from the radio's panadapter.
wait 5000
caption [box 22,1078,360,90] Zoom out and in, the whole Band, and B/S to hide the band and step rows for a taller waterfall.
wait 6000
caption [box 1203,1078,176,90] + Slice adds a receiver, + Pan a second panadapter.
wait 4500
caption [box 16,1186,1362,86] Step buttons tune down and up, 1 Hz to 1 kHz a tap.
wait 4500
caption [box 16,1283,1362,124] Macros (voice keyer, CW and more) and a large PTT.
wait 4500
caption [box 1390,68,520,1345] The controls in twelve sections. On a tablet they stay beside the display; on a phone they open as a drawer.
wait 6000
caption [box 880,0,1041,58] The network quality, Radio Setup, the Manual, the app's Log and Disconnect.
wait 5500
caption -
caption # Tuning
caption Tap the spectrum to tune there; drag it to tune smoothly.
tapmhz 14.2175
wait 3500
tapmhz 14.2190
wait 3500
caption The step buttons: one step a tap, and they keep stepping while held.
taptext +1k
wait 1500
taptext +100
wait 1500
taptext -100
wait 1500
taptext -1k
wait 2000
caption Tap STEP to choose the tuning step.
tapname stepButton
wait 4000
close
wait 1000
caption Tap the frequency to type one, on the keypad or a keyboard.
caption !mark 240,145
frequency-dialog
wait 2500
keys 7.155
wait 2500
keys <Enter>
wait 3500
caption Now on 40 m. Tap the mode for the list of modes: LSB, the sideband of the low bands.
caption !mark 560,115
popup modeChooser
wait 2500
taptext LSB ~369,155
wait 2000
caption Tap the filter width for the filter choices: 2.9k for phone.
caption !mark 933,115
popup filterChooser
wait 2500
taptext 2.9k
wait 2000
close
wait 1000
caption A band button goes back to where you were on that band.
taptext 20m
wait 5000
caption The band stack brings back that band's own filter too: 2.9k again for phone.
caption !mark 933,115
popup filterChooser
wait 2000
taptext 2.9k
wait 2000
close
wait 1000
caption -
caption # Receiving
caption RF gain: tap its tag on the spectrum.
tapname rfGainLabel
wait 4500
close
wait 1000
caption AGC: its mode, AGC-T, and Auto.
caption !mark 1042,115
popup agcChooser
wait 5000
close
wait 1000
caption The RX antenna; the TX antenna is beside it.
caption !mark 833,115
popup rxAntennaChooser
wait 4500
close
wait 1000
caption The slice's volume, and the radio's own line out.
caption !mark 1125,115
popup volumePopup
wait 4500
close
wait 1000
caption Tap the DSP flags for the filter widths and the DSP switches: NR on, and off again.
taptext NR ~600,126
wait 3000
taptext NR ~543,401
wait 3500
taptext NR ~543,401
wait 2500
close
wait 1000
caption SPLIT: a tap turns split on and off; press and hold for a second slice or XIT, and the offset.
holdname splitHit
wait 4500
close
wait 1000
caption -
caption # Meters
caption Tap a meter for the choices: S-meter, dBm, voltage, temperature, ALC and more, analog or as bars.
tapname meterLeft
wait 5500
close
wait 1000
caption While you transmit, the meters show power, SWR and the microphone.
preview-tx on
wait 5000
preview-tx off
wait 1000
caption -
caption # Slices
caption + Slice adds a receiver on the same panadapter: slice B. Each slice has its own volume and Mute: B muted here, so A's station is heard alone.
taptext + Slice
wait 800
caption !mark 1125,115
popup volumePopup
wait 1000
taptext Mute ~824,351
wait 2500
close
wait 1500
slices
caption Tap the spectrum to tune the active slice: B moves, A stays on the station.
tapmhz 14.2225
wait 4500
caption Each slice has its chip, its flag on the spectrum, its own mode, filter and volume.
wait 5500
caption Tap a chip to make that slice active.
tapname sliceChipA
wait 3500
tapname sliceChipB
wait 3500
caption Press and hold a chip: Make TX slice, or Close slice.
holdname sliceChipB
wait 3500
caption Close slice removes it. A stays the TX slice, with the red TX tag.
taptext Close slice
wait 4000
slices
closeslice B
slice A
wait 1500
caption -
caption # The controls
caption Tap a section to show it beside the display; several can show at once.
taptext DSP ~1021,82
wait 4500
taptext View ~1324,82
wait 2500
caption DSP: noise reduction and blanking, notches and the radio's DSP settings.
wait 4000
taptext Audio ~1081,82
taptext DSP ~1021,82
caption Audio: where the sound comes from and goes to, and the levels.
wait 5000
taptext TX ~1142,82
taptext Audio ~1081,82
caption TX: power, tune power, the microphone, VOX, the transmit lock and split.
wait 5000
taptext eSSB ~1203,82
taptext TX ~1142,82
caption eSSB: the TX filter, equaliser and the microphone chain.
wait 5000
taptext CW ~1263,82
taptext eSSB ~1203,82
caption CW: speed, paddles, the decoder, autotune and CW memories.
wait 5000
taptext Prof ~1021,141
taptext CW ~1263,82
caption Prof: the radio's profiles, and App setups for the app's own settings.
wait 5000
taptext Mem ~1081,141
taptext Prof ~1021,141
caption Mem: the radio's memories.
wait 4500
taptext Log ~1142,141
taptext Mem ~1081,141
caption Log: the QSO log, callsign lookup, and logbooks such as QRZ.com and Wavelog.
wait 5000
taptext FTx ~1203,141
taptext Log ~1142,141
caption FTx: FT8 and FT4 in the app itself, no computer needed.
wait 5000
taptext FreeDV ~1263,141
taptext FTx ~1203,141
caption FreeDV: RADE and FreeDV digital voice.
wait 5000
taptext Digi ~1324,141
taptext FreeDV ~1263,141
caption Digi: RTTY and PSK.
wait 5000
taptext View ~1324,82
taptext Digi ~1324,141
caption View: Big buttons, the band plan, text size and the display.
wait 5000
caption -
caption # Radio Setup
caption !cut
taptext Setup
wait 900
click setupTab1
wait 900
caption !uncut
caption Radio Setup holds the radio's own settings, as in SmartSDR. Transmit: what the radio sends on each band.
wait 5500
click setupTab3
caption Audio: the radio's audio settings.
wait 4500
click setupTab4
caption RX: the receiver's settings.
wait 4500
click setupTab7
caption Amp: amplifiers, tuners and antenna switches.
wait 4500
click setupTab8
caption USB: the radio's USB cables for CAT, band data and serial ports.
wait 4500
click setupTab9
caption MIDI: a controller as a VFO knob and buttons.
wait 4500
close
wait 1200
caption -
caption # Macros and Big buttons
caption Macros: voice keyer slots, CW memories and more, one tap away.
tapname macrosButton
wait 5000
tapname macrosButton
wait 1200
caption Big buttons: large controls for the car, gloves or a quick look. Hold Exit to leave.
tapname bigButtonsOpen
wait 6500
holdname bigExit
wait 1500
caption -
record off
slices
freq 14.074
mode DIGU
wait 1500
slices
